  "classification": "Validated public weight aggregate can overflow during weighted calculation; supported production reachability and behavior remain unproven.",
  "trace": [
    "WeaponSkillDistribution exposes nine f32 weights and derives deserialization. validate checks each finite and nonnegative and checks the relevant family and overall totals are positive, but does not require normalized weights or finite aggregate products. With sword = f32::MAX, all other weights zero, melee=true and ranged=false, those checks are true; a weighted_check closure returning 2.0 produces a product exceeding the finite f32 maximum before division. This is a source-level representable counterexample, not a product execution.",
    "The authored item validator instead requires finite nonnegative source weights with an f64 sum within 0.0001 of 1 and matching weapon families; the build script invokes that validation before emitting the embedded item catalog. Catalog weights are copied into the persisted Item record; one inspected strategic equipment projection and several combat consumers read the distribution. This supports a bounded authored path but does not prove every constructor, stored-value admission, producer or caller is bounded.",
    "The owner also maps nonfinite and negative raw weights to zero in weights() and has a zero-total fallback. Any repair must consider whether arbitrary positive relative weights are intentionally supported and preserve existing normalization of very small positive weights, unarmed behavior and deterministic gameplay for supported values. No present authored weapon with extreme weights is claimed."
  ],
  "repair_direction": "Trace all construction and storage paths, whether validate is required at each boundary, and all consumers; choose whether the contract is normalized or arbitrary positive relative weights and make aggregate arithmetic safe for that contract. Preserve supported weapon skills and avoid compatibility fields or migrations.",
  "later_acceptance": [
    "After separately authorized repair, verify normalized catalog values, tiny positive weights, zero distributions, finite extremes and invalid admissions across tactical and strategic consumers."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Prove supported reachability, reconcile historical aliases and finish every connected lens. No product build, tests or runtime probes were performed."
  ],
  "discovery_status": "partial; source-level counterexample to the public validation/calculation combination, not an observed gameplay failure",
  "repair_status": "not started",
  "validation_status": "not performed"
}
